## Fabric widths

Most fabrics sold in India come in two common widths:

| Width | Approx. cm | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 44 inch | ~112 cm | Common for cotton, silk, brocade and many traditional fabrics |
| 58 inch | ~147 cm | Common for georgette, crepe, synthetics and many modern fabrics |

Wider fabric usually means fewer metres for the same garment.

