## Using the JSON data

The file `data/requirements.json` contains the same estimates in a structured format.

Example in JavaScript:

```js
import data from "./data/requirements.json" assert { type: "json" };

function estimate(garmentId, width = "58in") {
  const item = data.garments.find((g) => g.id === garmentId);
  if (!item) throw new Error(`Unknown garment: ${garmentId}`);
  const [min, max] = item.metres[width];
  return `${item.name}: ${min}–${max} m (${width} width)`;
}

console.log(estimate("anarkali", "44in"));
// Anarkali: 4–6 m (44in width)
```

